# Every seeded example on a surface in this repo — the grey text in an empty
# field, and any element marked `data-example` — and where it came from. Held by
# `example-check.mjs`; that file says why this is a declared list and not a rule
# about content (an invented plan and a real one are the same sentence).
#
# An example taken from somebody's actual work is not declarable and never
# becomes declarable. Invent the scenario. The plan walk shipped four examples
# lifted from a live plan of the owner's, on a public site, because they were the
# plan in front of the session that built the page.
#
#   file | invented | product-copy | public-data | the example's opening words
#
#   invented     — a scenario made up for the page, resembling nobody's real work
#   product-copy — the app's own strings, quoted back as a sample
#   public-data  — a row from a published dataset, under its terms
#
